tests.measures:
For each chooser and design:
- the probability of at least one cycle among strict occasions (C);
- the probability of a P1 violation;
- the counts of strict occasions and of P1-testable occasions;
- the false-strict rate of the stability rule;
- Selten's predictive success: the one-order class's pass rate minus the share of all choice patterns it allows.

Per chooser:
- strict share, invalid share and first-position share;
- C on the per-presentation family and on the aggregated family;
- P1 violations and forced-top accuracy;
- picks on unjoined pairs, descriptive only;
- at default temperature, binary choice frequencies with an order-constrained test of a mixture of orders (a periphery measure that carries no RF1 verdict).
